commit 2a2bdf4c2b2c0c544614fc368fa3ce56d548ce14
Author: GoodOlClint <goodolclint@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 18:29:35 2026 -0500

    Implement Gemma 4 E-series MTP centroid embedder (use_ordered_embeddings) (#383)
    
    Implement Gemma 4 E-series MTP centroid embedder, then fix it for quantized drafters
    
    Gemma4AssistantMaskedEmbedder.callAsFunction was a fatalError stub, trapping the whole E-series MTP path (E2B/E4B drafters use `use_ordered_embeddings=true`). Ported the centroid-routed sparse LM head from mlx-vlm's masked_embedder.py: score 2048 clusters, keep top-K, gather those token rows from the tied embedding, score them, and scatter back to full vocab with unselected positions masked below the selected minimum. mask_value stays on-device (no `.item()` sync in the per-token loop). 26B-A4B/31B drafters (`use_ordered_embeddings=false`) are unaffected.
    
    Follow-up fix: the initial version gathered rows from the tied embedding's raw `.weight`, which is packed for a `QuantizedEmbedding` (the format every mlx-community E-series assistant actually ships in), causing a reshape crash on first drafter forward — only unquantized bf16 drafters worked. Fixed by gathering rows through the embedding module's forward instead of its raw weight, so both plain and quantized embeddings return correctly shaped (dequantized) rows.
    
    Tests:
    - `testMaskedEmbedderSelectedLogitsMatchDense` — correctness pin against dense logits with identity token_ordering.
    - TEST_E{2,4}B_PAIR integration tests updated to assert healthy speculation instead of the old fatalError trap.
    - `testMaskedEmbedderQuantizedTiedEmbedding` — regression pin for quantized tied embeddings (crashes on the old raw-`.weight` path).
    - Both pins now set `token_ordering` via `update(parameters:)` rather than direct `@ParameterInfo` assignment.
    
    Tracks ml-explore/mlx-swift-lm#279. Reported by @mandrael.

