commit f1573a93129d7ace758b62efe9b46d16efafb52a
Author: ctymoszek <31750745+ctymoszek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 10:57:31 2026 -0400

    Add MLXFoundationModels: an MLX-backed FoundationModels LanguageModel (#334)
    
    Add MLXFoundationModels: an MLX-backed FoundationModels LanguageModel
    
    MLXLanguageModel conforms to FoundationModels.LanguageModel, allowing a local MLX model to work with LanguageModelSession. It is built from a ModelConfiguration and loaded through mlx-swift-lm's existing model factory, so any architecture the package already runs is reachable through FoundationModels. A model's capabilities — .guidedGeneration, .toolCalling, .reasoning, .vision — are declared at construction.
    
    A new standalone library, MLXGuidedGeneration, constrains any MLX model's output to a JSON Schema, EBNF grammar, or structural tag by masking token logits at each decoding step. It uses a vendored, namespace-isolated copy of XGrammar (the MLXCXGrammar C++ target), with no FoundationModels dependency. It runs on macOS 14 / iOS 17 and later.
    
    The FoundationModels adapter is gated by one default-on SwiftPM trait, FoundationModelsIntegration, and is available on iOS/macOS/visionOS 27.0 (canImport(FoundationModels, _version: 2)). With the trait turned off, or when building against an older SDK, MLXFoundationModels compiles to an empty module and the vendored XGrammar C++ is not built. The package's minimum OS versions are unchanged from upstream.
    
    A #huggingFaceLanguageModel macro fills in the HuggingFace download and tokenizer setup. The MLXLanguageModel initializer can be used directly to provide a path to locally stored weights, or a different downloader or tokenizer.
    
    Co-authored-by: Cori Tymoszek Park 31750745+ctymoszek@users.noreply.github.com
    Co-authored-by: Christopher Webb 207731778+thechriswebb@users.noreply.github.com

