commit 65be34c64237c0b5da348169d3a9b59f37453fe2
Author: spokvulcan <ivanchenko.b@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 14 18:45:35 2026 +0300

    Qwen3.5/3.6: windowed prefill + state-threaded warm continuation (fixes multi-turn M-RoPE drift) (#399)
    
    feat(vlm): windowed prefill for Qwen3.5/3.6, with warm cross-turn continuation
    
    Adds chunked ("windowed") prefill for Qwen3.5, bounding attention scratch to `[heads, window, L]` instead of `[heads, L, L]`, which was OOMing on long image prompts. Batched inputs still use the single-shot path.
    
    `LanguageModel.prepare` now threads an optional `LMOutput.State` (M-RoPE position state) through, so Qwen3.5 can continue an already-warmed KV cache across turns instead of resetting rope positions to zero. `ChatSession`/`TokenIterator` persist this state across turns and tool-call restarts. Other model conformers accept and ignore the parameter.
    
    This also fixes a live cross-turn bug: since M-RoPE state wasn't previously carried between turns, warm continuations silently recomputed positions from scratch, causing measurable logit drift (0.43 max-abs vs. a 8.3e-07 noise floor) on repeated turns with images.
    
    Other changes:
    - `getRopeIndex` supports an offset-aware `positionOffset` for computing new-image rope positions from a warm cache's anchor.
    - Vision-embedding preamble factored into `visionInputEmbeddings`, shared across prepare paths.
    - Windowed loop uses `asyncEval` per chunk + trailing eval (matches Gemma3's chunked-prefill pattern).
    - `Qwen3VLProcessorConfiguration` now decodes new-style `size.{longest_edge,shortest_edge}` pixel budgets, fixing silent fallback for newer Qwen3-VL configs.
    - Added `Qwen35ContinuationTests` (5 tiny-model equivalence tests) and `Qwen3VLProcessorConfigTests`.

